From 1b24e50bc88f4e34cea1bffcd5a02edc56ccb383 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hayaksi1 <193020925+hayaksi1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 10:27:03 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Re-record the goldens of the views several branches change at
 once

The snapshot policy keeps the first branch's golden when two branches
record the same view, so every view touched by more than one branch
fails verification on the integrated tree: notification, advanced and
developer settings, the room list, the messages screen, the space view
and the login mode screen. Recorded on master after integration.

Views that render differently from run to run on this machine (share
location, PIN entry, QR code, blocked users, user status, the verified
user send failure sheet and a few others) keep upstream's goldens.

Fork-Feature: fork-tooling
